    "q-143894": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143894",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}, & 0<x<2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=\\sqrt[3]{X},$ use the change-of-variables method to find the probability density function of $Y.$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X\\in (a,b)$ is a continuous random variable with probability density function ${f}_{X}$ and $Y=u(X),$ where the function $u(x)$ is strictly monotonic, then according to the change-of-variables method, the probability density function of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}({u}^{-1}(y))\\cdot |({u}^{-1})^{′}(y)|, & y\\text{ is between }u(a)\\text{ and }u(b) \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $Y=\\sqrt[3]{X}.$ The transformation $u(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}$ is strictly monotonically *increasing*, so the change-of-variables method can be used.\n\nFirst, we find ${u}^{-1}(y)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(y) & =\\sqrt[3]{y} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{-1}(y)} \\\\ {u}^{-1}(y) & ={y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find $({u}^{-1})^{′}(y):$\n\n$$\n({u}^{-1})^{′}(y)=3{y}^{2}\n$$\n\nAccording to the change-of-variables method, for nonzero ${f}_{Y},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={f}_{X}({u}^{-1}(y))\\cdot |({u}^{-1})^{′}(y)| \\\\  & ={f}_{X}({y}^{3})\\cdot |3{y}^{2}| \\\\  & =\\frac{{({y}^{3})}^{3}}{4}\\cdot 3{y}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{9}}{4}\\cdot 3{y}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{y}^{11}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${f}_{X}$ is nonzero on $0<x<2,$ the bounds are $a=0$ and $b=2,$ we have\n\n$$\nu(0)=0,\\,u(2)=\\sqrt[3]{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability distribution of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{y}^{11}}{4}, & 0<y<\\sqrt[3]{2} \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-143894-a",
              "type": "math",
